note: 6 object(s) need a library ROOT/ does not ship and were not checked;
      test/check-rootfs-deps.py reports which.
UNRESOLVED symbols in ROOT/:

  usr/bin/app
      foo_new
      foo_v2
  usr/bin/app1
      foo_new
      foo_v2
  usr/bin/app2
      foo_new
      foo_v2
  usr/bin/app3
      foo_new
      foo_v2
  usr/bin/app4
      foo_new
      foo_v2
  usr/bin/app5
      foo_new
      foo_v2
  usr/bin/app6
      foo_new
      foo_v2
  usr/bin/usesmany
      many_1
      many_2
      many_3
      many_4
      many_5
      many_6
      ... and 3 more

Each of these calls a function that no library in its NEEDED closure defines, and
will fail with 'undefined symbol' when the call is first made. The usual cause is a
header from builder/deps.txt newer than the library packages/ ships: bump ours to
at least sid's (docs/guides/linking.md). A plugin that expects its host program to
provide the symbol is not a bug; add it to test/known-unresolved-symbols.txt.
